   577→        then: starts in background, writes PID file, returns immediately with status message
   578→      - id: ac-3
   579→        given: daemon not running
   580→        when: kspec serve --port 8080 executed
   581→        then: starts on specified port
   582→      - id: ac-4
   583→        given: daemon running
   584→        when: kspec serve stop executed
   585→        then: sends SIGTERM to daemon PID, waits for clean shutdown, removes PID file
   586→      - id: ac-5
   587→        given: daemon not running
   588→        when: kspec serve stop executed
   589→        then: outputs 'Daemon not running' with exit code 0 (idempotent)
   590→      - id: ac-6
   591→        given: any state
   592→        when: kspec serve status executed
   593→        then: outputs JSON with {running, pid, port, uptime, connections}
   594→      - id: ac-7
   595→        given: daemon running
   596→        when: kspec serve restart executed
   597→        then: stops existing daemon, starts new one, preserves port setting
   598→      - id: ac-8
   599→        given: any state
   600→        when: kspec serve logs executed
   601→        then: tails daemon log file (.kspec/.daemon.log)
   602→      - id: ac-9
   603→        given: daemon running
   604→        when: kspec serve logs --follow executed
   605→        then: streams log output continuously until Ctrl+C
   606→      - id: ac-10
   607→        given: port already in use
   608→        when: kspec serve attempts to start
   609→        then: fails with clear error message suggesting --port flag
   610→

